# .cursorrules — Sebastien Henry portfolio (2026 H1)
# Applies to ALL 9 portfolio repos under github.com/SebAustin/*. Per-repo
# .cursorrules files extend (not replace) these.

## 1. Identity
You are pair-programming with Sebastien Henry — a senior engineer with 19 years
of experience. He makes architecture decisions; you generate code. Do NOT ask
clarifying questions about scope already specified. Do NOT narrate. Implement
exactly what is asked, then stop.

## 2. Stack (2026-current, non-negotiable)
- Python 3.12. uv 0.5+ for dependency management. ruff 0.7+. mypy --strict.
- pydantic v2.9+. FastAPI 0.115+. pytest 8+. httpx 0.28+ (never `requests`).
- LangGraph 1.x (StateGraph, PostgresSaver, interrupt). LangChain 1.x.
- Anthropic SDK ≥ 0.40 (Claude Sonnet 4.5 / Opus 4.7, Citations API enabled).
- MCP spec 2025-11-25. Official `mcp` Python SDK 1.x; FastMCP 2.x for ergonomics.
- Snowflake Cortex GA features as of May 2026 only.
- Terraform 1.10+ / OpenTofu 1.8+. AWS provider 6.x. Google provider 6.x.
- Solidity 0.8.26. Foundry only (no Hardhat). solc pinned in foundry.toml.

## 3. Type safety
- Every public function has full type hints. Every pydantic model uses
  `model_config = ConfigDict(extra="forbid")` where appropriate.
- `mypy --strict src/` must pass before any PR is merged.
- No `# type: ignore` without a one-line comment explaining why.

## 4. Testing
- Every module has matching tests under `tests/unit/`.
- `pytest-asyncio` in `strict` mode. Network mocked with `respx`.
- Coverage gate: 85% line coverage on `src/`.
- Integration tests marked `@pytest.mark.integration` and skipped by default.

## 5. Evals
- Every project has an `evals/` directory with one runnable harness.
- Eval output is JSONL (one row per case, summary row last).
- Every metric is numeric. LLM-as-judge is paired with at least one deterministic
  metric (exec-accuracy, F1, recall@k, NDCG@k, latency).
- CI runs a smoke slice on every PR and posts the delta as a sticky comment.

## 6. Forbidden patterns
- `print()` in library code (use `structlog` or `logging`).
- Bare `except:` — always name the exception.
- `subprocess.run(shell=True)` — never.
- Inline JSON strings for IAM / SQL DDL — use data sources / DSLs.
- Hardcoded credentials, account IDs, project IDs. Use env + pydantic-settings.
- `from langgraph.prebuilt import create_react_agent` shortcuts — always
  explicit `StateGraph` for auditability.
- LLM-generated security-critical decisions (sanctions matching, refund
  approval, swap blocking) without a deterministic rule firing first.

## 7. Citations contract
- Anywhere user-facing claims reference source documents (RAG, SAR memos, match
  rationales, adverse media findings), the Anthropic Citations API is enabled
  (`citations={"enabled": True}`) and every text block in the response must
  carry citations. Uncited claims are dropped or tagged `[INFERENCE]`.

## 8. Reproducibility
- All random seeds set. `PYTHONHASHSEED=0` in containers. Sort everything that
  iterates in order-dependent code.
- Pin every direct dependency. Pin Docker base images by sha256 digest, not tag.
- Each eval result records: git SHA, model id, judge model id, harness version,
  host info, wall-clock, token counts, $ cost.

## 9. Documentation
- Every repo: README.md with a Mermaid architecture diagram, eval table with
  numeric targets, and 3–5 source citations to real 2026 specs/papers/blog posts.
- Every architectural decision deviating from defaults gets an ADR in `docs/adr/`
  using MADR format.
- Conventional commits. PR descriptions reference an issue and include the
  eval delta JSON.

## 10. When in doubt
Prefer the more conservative, more verbose, more logged path. These repos will
be read by Anthropic / Cursor / Snowflake hiring managers. Trust is the product.

# ============================================================================
# PROJECT DELTAS — mcp-financial-data
# ============================================================================

## P1. MCP spec compliance
- Target: MCP spec 2025-11-25. The server is a streamable-HTTP MCP server
  (NOT stdio) because it is also an OAuth 2.1 resource server. Capability
  advertisement at startup uses the latest schema version.
- Every tool registered with `FastMCP` has: a typed pydantic input model, a
  typed pydantic output model, a docstring (becomes the tool description),
  and a structured-log line at start + end.

## P2. SEC EDGAR Fair Access compliance (HARD)
- Every EDGAR HTTP request MUST include the User-Agent header sourced from
  `EDGAR_USER_AGENT` env var, formatted "Name <contact@example.com>". A
  request without a contact UA is a hard failure (raise; do not fall back).
- Rate limit ≤ 10 req/sec across the process. Use `asyncio.Semaphore` +
  `tenacity` exponential backoff on 429.
- Cache responses for ≥ 24 h locally (Postgres or SQLite) so repeat eval runs
  do not pound the EDGAR endpoint.

## P3. Citations are non-optional in the 10-K extractor
- `extractors/tenk.py` calls Claude Sonnet 4.5 with `citations={"enabled": True}`
  on every document block (per Anthropic Citations API).
- The output type `CitedClaim` carries `text: str` AND `citations: list[Citation]`.
- Any model-generated text returned WITHOUT a `citations` array is either
  dropped or wrapped in `[INFERENCE]` and demoted to a `notes` field — never
  surfaced as a fact.
- Tests verify: (a) shape, (b) at least one citation per fact in fixtures.

## P4. OAuth 2.1 resource-server scope
- This repo IS the resource server, not the IdP. Validate JWT against
  `MCP_OAUTH_JWKS_URL`, audience = `MCP_OAUTH_AUDIENCE`, required scopes
  from `MCP_OAUTH_REQUIRED_SCOPES`.
- Tokens are validated on every request (no caching beyond JWKS public-key
  rotation TTL). PKCE is enforced for any /authorize round-trip we expose.
- A failing token check returns RFC 6750 `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error=...`
  with the exact error spec keywords (`invalid_token`, `insufficient_scope`).

## P5. Spend cap
- `MAX_API_SPEND_USD` env var is read at process start. The 10-K extractor and
  the eval harness both increment a process-local counter and refuse new calls
  when the cap is hit. CI defaults to `--offline` so this never fires there.

## P6. Offline-first development
- Every external client (EDGAR, FRED, Polygon, Anthropic) is fronted by a
  thin port (`Protocol`) so tests inject `respx` mocks. The eval harness
  takes `--offline` to use canned fixtures and a deterministic stub judge.

## P7. Streamable HTTP not stdio
- The server is launched with `python -m mcp_financial_data.server` and
  binds to `MCP_HOST:MCP_PORT`. Local-only stdio mode is OUT of scope for
  this project — pick the support-agent project (P6) if stdio is needed.

## P8. Anchor company audience
- Every Cursor-generated file in this repo will be read by an Anthropic FDE,
  Bridgewater / Citadel quant, or a Cursor founder. Optimize for: clear types,
  one-screen functions, every sketch-y assumption captured in a NOTE comment
  with a TODO and a prompt link.
